  "result": "`slugify(text)` now works in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes (12 tests, 0 failed).\n\nIt follows your rules in this order:\n- `đ` and `Đ` become `d`.\n- Other diacritics are stripped (Vietnamese and other Latin text).\n- The text is lowercased.\n- Each run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes a single hyphen.\n- Leading and trailing hyphens are removed.\n- The result is cut to 50 characters, and any hyphen left at the end of the cut is removed.\n\nI added 10 `slugify` tests to `test/strings.test.js`, below the two `capitalize` tests. They cover:\n- basic hyphenation\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics\n- `đ`/`Đ`\n- runs of symbols\n- trimming\n- empty and symbol-only input\n- the 50-character cut, including a cut that lands on a hyphen and one that doesn't\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
